      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "•\tSTREAMS TODO",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tstream read and write new parameter ThrowIfWouldBlock",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tnew method to bool inputstream::IsDataAvailable (timeout = 0) – returns true asap, but waits up time timeout secondsds if value was false. Doesn’t throw",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tMaybe add to stream writer WouldWriteBlock(nbytes = 1)? – but unclear if useful/owrth it.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tDocument that streamns are thread safe, but assume others are too, and so don’t hav wide blocks to assure underlying synconicity. They are safe – but not serializers.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tConsidered adding read/write timeout params to objects – and might make sense – but document decided this appears structurally better (but reconsider later – migh twork for sockets).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
